        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Align on customer interaction script and quick training approach",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M34",
            "speaker_id": 486514,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Okay team, let's tackle T4. I've put together a first draft of the customer interaction script for A3. The idea is to have a few simple, friendly lines to engage customers. Feedback is welcome!\nDraft: 'Hi, have you seen our new seasonal promotion? We have some great gift ideas.'",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T4",
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M35",
            "speaker_id": 72026,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "I don't know, I feel weird using a script. It sounds unnatural.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M36",
            "speaker_id": 398662,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "The opening is okay. Maybe we can add a question to it? Like 'Are you looking for a gift for anyone special?'",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M37",
            "speaker_id": 318034,
            "reply_to": "M36",
            "text": "The risk with a direct question like that is a 'no' answer, which ends the conversation. A better approach might be an open-ended, observation-based question, like 'I see you're looking at the candles. The spiced apple scent is the most popular one this week.' It invites conversation without pressure.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "brain",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M38",
            "speaker_id": 475166,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "That's a fantastic point, @318034. And @72026, you're right, it shouldn't sound robotic. Let's think of this less as a 'script' and more as a collection of 'helpful talking points'. We can each use what feels natural.",
            "mentions": [
              318034,
              72026
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 486514,
            "reply_to": "M38",
            "text": "Okay, I love that feedback. I'll rewrite it as a 'talking points' guide. It will include:\n1. An opening line (e.g., 'Feel free to browse our new seasonal corner').\n2. Product-specific hooks (like @318034's candle example).\n3. A pairing suggestion (e.g., 'This mug would be perfect with our hot chocolate mix').\nHow does that sound for our final A3?",
            "mentions": [
              318034
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 4
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 352698,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "That's a much better approach. It gives us flexibility.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 475166,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "Decision made. Now, to make sure we're all comfortable, we should do a quick practice session as planned in T8. A 15-minute role-play should be enough. When's a good time for everyone?",
